# 25. TESTING REQUIREMENTS

Before considering the project complete, test all core workflows.

TEST 1: Registration
- Create a seller account.
- Create a buyer account.
- Verify that both users can log in independently.

TEST 2: Product Listing
- Seller creates a tomato listing.
- Product persists in the database.
- Product appears in the marketplace.

TEST 3: Cross-Device Visibility
- Open the deployed site in another browser or on another device.
- Log in as a buyer.
- Verify that the tomato listing appears without manually entering it again.

TEST 4: Live Bidding
- Buyer submits an offer.
- Seller receives the bid in real time.
- Buyer sees the correct bid status.

TEST 5: Competing Offers
- Two different buyers submit bids.
- Seller can compare both offers.
- Seller can accept the preferred offer.

TEST 6: Order Creation
- Seller accepts a bid.
- Exactly one valid order is created.
- Both buyer and seller see the same order.

TEST 7: Inventory
- Reserve part of a product's quantity.
- Verify that remaining available inventory is correct.
- Attempt an order exceeding available stock.
- Confirm that the backend rejects it.

TEST 8: Sold Status
- Complete the sale of all available inventory.
- Confirm that the product becomes SOLD OUT.
- Verify that it cannot be purchased again.
- Verify that its order history remains available.

TEST 9: Permissions
- Attempt to edit another seller's listing as a buyer.
- Confirm that the backend denies the operation.
- Attempt to read another user's private notifications.
- Confirm that the backend denies the operation.

TEST 10: Image Upload
- Upload a product image.
- Refresh the page.
- Confirm that the image remains available.

TEST 11: Messaging
- Send a message from buyer to seller.
- Confirm that only authorized conversation participants can access it.

TEST 12: Location
- Add a seller's location.
- Verify that the listing appears in the location view when discoverability is enabled.

TEST 13: Responsive Design
- Test desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts.

TEST 14: Production Build
- Run the production build.
- Fix compilation errors.
- Fix broken routes.
- Fix missing environment configuration.
- Fix runtime errors and major console warnings.

